Let $\displaystyle d = k$.
From $\displaystyle \frac{c}{d} = 6$, we have $\displaystyle c = 6d = 6k$.
From $\displaystyle \frac{b}{c} = \frac{1}{3}$, we have $\displaystyle b = \frac{1}{3}c = \frac{1}{3}(6k) = 2k$.
From $\displaystyle \frac{a}{b} = 4$, we have $\displaystyle a = 4b = 4(2k) = 8k$.
