We can compute $\text{{J}}(2,12,9)$ directly using the given definition. \begin{align*}
\text{{J}}(2,12,9) &= \frac{2}{12} + \frac{12}{9} + \frac{9}{2} \\
&= \frac{1}{6} + \frac{4}{3} + \frac{9}{2}.
\end{align*}
To add these fractions, we need a common denominator. The least common denominator of 6, 3, and 2 is 6. \begin{align*}
\frac{1}{6} + \frac{4}{3} + \frac{9}{2} &= \frac{1}{6} + \frac{8}{6} + \frac{27}{6} \\
&= \frac{1 + 8 + 27}{6} \\
&= \frac{36}{6} \\
&= 6.
\end{align*} Thus, the value of $\text{{J}}(2,12,9)$ is 6. \boxed{6}

