To expand the product of $(x+3)(x-8)$, we use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials):
\begin{align*}
(x+3)(x-8) &= x \cdot x + x \cdot (-8) + 3 \cdot x + 3 \cdot (-8) \\
&= x^2 - 8x + 3x - 24
\end{align*}
Next, we combine the like terms (-8x and 3x):
\begin{align*}
x^2 - 8x + 3x - 24 &= x^2 - 5x - 24
\end{align*}
Thus, the expanded product is \boxed{x^2 - 5x - 24}.

