answer_1:
The circumference of the circle is $12\pi$ inches, so the radius is $\frac{12\pi}{2\pi}=6$ inches.

The measure of $\angle TXZ$ is $60^{\circ}$, so the length of $XZ$ is $6\sin 60^{\circ} = 6\left(\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right) = 3\sqrt{3}$ inches.

\boxed{3\sqrt{3}}

