We use the rule of Sarrus for a \(3\times 3\) determinant: \[\begin{vmatrix} a & b & c \\ d & e & f \\ g & h & i \end{vmatrix} = aei + bfg + cdh - ceg - bdi - afh.\]Apply to our matrix: \(a=1,\;b=-3,\;c=3,\;d=0,\;e=5,\;f=-1,\;g=4,\;h=-2,\;i=1.\) \[ \begin{aligned} aei &= 1\cdot 5\cdot 1 = 5, \\ bfg &= (-3)(-1)(4) = 12, \\ cdh &= 0\cdot (-2)\cdot 3 = 0, \\ ceg &= 3\cdot 5\cdot (-1) = -15, \\ bdi &= (-3)\cdot 0\cdot 1 = 0, \\ afh &= (-3)\cdot (-1)\cdot 4 = 12. \end{aligned} \] Summing: \[ 5 + 12 + 0 - (-15) - 0 - 12 = 5 + 12 + 15 - 12 = 20. \] Thus the determinant is \boxed{20}.\[
\boxed{20}
\]

